  "title": "Provider-neutral Forge seam with a GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Introduces a provider-neutral `forge` module: a `Forge` trait (branch, pull request, status block, review, check status, head commit, capabilities), a pure `report_change` step that runs those calls in one fixed order, and an in-memory `FakeForge` double. A new `github` module is the first adapter, wrapping the existing `gh` command-line work behind the trait, and `main.rs` rewires `review post`, `pr status apply`, `pr status refresh` and `--post-to` to go through the forge instead of calling `gh` directly. `pr_status` loses its process code and gains a `run` method on `GhClient` plus a `parse_checks`/`gates_from_checks` split, and a new `osf forge pr open` command opens a pull request through the adapter.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
